  "goodToKnow": "Der Wohnungsmarkt is the housing market. In German cities like Munich, Berlin, Frankfurt and Hamburg, it's very angespannt (tight): rents have risen sharply, viewings attract crowds, and the Mietpreisbremse limits rents for new contracts. Around half of Germans rent, more than in most EU countries. Die Wohnungsnot is a housing shortage. Plural: die Wohnungsmärkte."
